The replacement stores the resolved `MESG*` directly in the lookup table, removing the per-call index-to-pointer conversion and the null-check branch after the lookup. This makes the common path a single pointer load and return.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const MESG* lookup[65536];
    static bool initialized = false;
    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; --i)
            lookup[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        initialized = true;
    }

    return lookup[num];
}
```